{
    "name": "LED Bargraph VU Meter (4-LED)",
    "description": "An LM3914-style audio level meter: a 1kHz audio signal with rising amplitude feeds an op-amp peak detector (22ms hold), whose envelope is compared against a 4-tap resistor reference ladder (0.5/1.5/2.5/3.5V) by 4 comparators, each driving an LED (3 green + 1 red peak LED). Run the transient — LEDs light cumulatively 1→2→3→4 as the level rises (~8.3mA green, 9.4mA red when lit). Like real bargraphs, the boundary LED flickers briefly at threshold (no hysteresis — faithful LM3914 behavior). (ngspice-validated: every window unambiguously lit/dark.)",
    "tags": ["display", "led", "bargraph", "vu-meter", "audio", "comparator", "sensor"],
    "analysisConfig": {
        "analysis": {
            "type": "tran",
            "stopTime": "80m",
            "stepTime": "20u"
        },
        "probes": ["i(R7)", "i(R8)", "i(R9)", "i(R10)", "v(level)", "v(env)"]
    },
